# a turn that may write a list, or run code that nobody has seen, may give the list other storage, another length or another kind. Then no row asks the list in front of the loop, and every read asks for itself
# the twin that is tested is list-of-numbers-is-added-up-with-storage-and-length-from-in-front-of-the-loop.ir: the same loop with nothing else in the turn
# f1 = grows, f2 = storesBehindTheEnd, f3 = setsTheLength, f4 = shrinks, f5 = changesTheKind, f6 = makesAHole, f7 = writesThroughAnotherName, f8 = callsACallee, f9 = readsAGetter, f10 = converts, f11 = takesAnotherList, f12 = callsAndNeverAsksTheLength
